[49m[38;5;10m+     1[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # CONFIGS.md — Phase B configuration-surface table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     2[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     3[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Mechanical derivation of the axes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There is exactly **one** public entry point (`c_src/include/lib.h`), and it is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m also the lowest-level one — the two internal helpers `cbLuminance` and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `cbContrastRatio` are `static`, so `contrast_ratio` is simultaneously the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m convenience wrapper *and* the deepest reachable entry point. There is nothing
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m lower to drive directly.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There are **no runtime options, modes, or flags**: no setter, no context
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m struct, no global state, no `#ifdef`, no `switch` (all greps = 0, see
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `ERRORS.md`). The entire branch surface of the library is:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Axis 1 — per-channel transfer branch** (3 ternaries in `cbLuminance`):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `C > 0.04045 ? pow((C+0.055)/1.055, 2.4) : C/12.92`, where `C = byte/255.f`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   Threshold: `0.04045 * 255 = 10.31475`, so byte `<= 10` → **linear** branch,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   byte `>= 11` → **pow** branch. Applied independently to R, G, B → **2^3 = 8
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   branch patterns per color**, and there are two colors → 64 pattern pairs.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Axis 2 — swap branch** (the single `if` in `cbContrastRatio`):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `LumA < LumB` (swap) / `LumA > LumB` (no swap) / `LumA == LumB` (no swap).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Axis 3 — divisor state** at the unguarded `High / Low`:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `Low > 0` / `Low == 0` (black) / both `0`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Axis 4 — channel value shape** within a branch: boundary bytes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `0, 1, 10, 11, 254, 255` vs interior values; per-channel isolation (only one
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   channel nonzero) exposes the individual `0.2126f / 0.7152f / 0.0722f`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   weights and the left-to-right single-precision accumulation order.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **Axis 5 — ABI shape**: the 3-byte `cb_rgb_255` is passed by value in one
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   x86-64 SysV INTEGER register; the 5 unused high bytes are a real input the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   caller controls.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Rows below are the cross-product of these axes, pruned to the combinations the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m C actually distinguishes. Every row is driven with **many randomized inputs**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m from a fixed-seed PRNG (a SplitMix64, seed `0x243F6A8885A308D3`) unless the row
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m is by definition a single point, and every row asserts **byte-for-byte**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (`to_bits()`) equality of the C and Rust return values, NaN included.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
